Work, knowledge, and social change (@work-knowledge-and-social-change: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_2FK3WWYVFYNV84AF1Z8PMWBZHP
This material investigates the organisation and transformation of work, expertise, science, technology, and collective life. It connects occupations, professions, workplaces, organisational cultures, authority, cooperation, conflict, and the social production of knowledge. Follow how skills are learned, how evidence or expertise becomes trusted, and how people sustain or contest technical systems. Link Ergon's production and maintenance accounts to Sociology, History, and Political-Economy, keeping the experience of participants and the assumptions of the explanation visible.

**Parent:** [Sociology](../Sociology.lingua#r_2ENBJ86RED2J0TCGJFZARTTNQT).
